  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to run",
      "items": [
        "cd rust && cargo run --release --bin hamiltonian -- --L 6 [--open 0|1]  (writes data/hamiltonian[_open]_L6.csv)",
        "cd julia && julia --project=. -t 16 clik.jl --L 6 --gamma 0.01 --backend dense|mps [--open 1] [--init scar] [--chi 64] [--expand-every 1]",
        "julia --project=. -t 8 forward_backward.jl --L 8 --gamma 0.1 --state minus-x [--channel z] [--chi 64] [--ref states.csv]",
        "julia --project=. lindblad_tdvp.jl L maxdims [gamma] [tmax] [dt] [cutoff]  (previous coefficients, data/)",
        "Analysis: python plot_scripts/plot_clik.py [dir]  (default data/used_data); python plot_scripts/compare_methods.py (also needs evolution_L<L>.csv from the old main binary)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Notes part",
      "items": [
        "Compile: latex/build_parts.sh tensor_networks → latex/parts/pdf/tensor_networks.pdf (full notes are built first; numbering as in latex/notes.tex)",
        "1 Model; 2 Theory; 2.1 Lindblad dynamics: forward and backward evolution",
        "3 How the simulations are done; 3.2 Pauli strings; 3.4 Density matrices: exact evolution in the Pauli basis",
        "3.13 Tensor networks: rho as an MPS, TDVP, influence matrix, CLIK; 12 Tensor-network and Krylov (CLIK) results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Key mechanics",
      "items": [
        "rho = 2^-L sum_P r_P P on PauliVec sites (1, sx, sy, sz); the Lindbladian is a real MPO",
        "CLIK: physical (real time) and traceless (complex time, angle alpha) states sampled every dt; Gram and projected L matrices, eigenvalues for nested T",
        "Forward/backward: rho with G, observable with G^T (H -> -H); <O>(t1 + t2) = o(t2).r(t1) / Tr rho(t1)",
        "Stepping: Taylor series with exact MPO applications below chi-switch, two-site TDVP with global Krylov expansion above"
      ]
    }
  ]
